## Architecture at a Glance

This project uses **Onion Architecture + CQRS + MVVM** on .NET {{project.dotnet.dotnetVersion}} WPF.

```
Presentation  ←  WPF Views, ViewModels (MVVM) — dispatches via MediatR
    ↓
Application   ←  Commands, Queries, Handlers (MediatR + FluentValidation)
    ↓
Domain        ←  Aggregates, Value Objects, Domain Events, Repository Interfaces
    ↓
Infrastructure ← Persistence (EF Core{{#if project.dotnet.hasPersistence}} SQLite{{/if}}), External Adapters
    ↓
Common        ←  Primitives, Result<T>, PagedList<T>, base types — no dependencies
```

**Layer rules:**
- Common has zero dependencies.
- Domain depends on Common only.
- Application depends on Domain + Common only.
- Infrastructure depends on Application + Domain + Common.
- Presentation depends on Application + Infrastructure + Common.
- Cross-layer shortcuts are forbidden.

## MVVM Pattern

```csharp
// ViewModel dispatches commands via MediatR
public partial class OrdersViewModel : ViewModelBase
{
    [ObservableProperty] private IReadOnlyList<OrderDto> _orders = [];

    [RelayCommand(CanExecute = nameof(IsNotBusy))]
    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        IsBusy = true;
        Orders = await _mediator.Send(new GetOrdersQuery());
        IsBusy = false;
    }
    private bool IsNotBusy => !IsBusy;
}
```

## CQRS Pattern

```csharp
// Handler in Application layer
public sealed class GetOrdersQueryHandler : IRequestHandler<GetOrdersQuery, IReadOnlyList<OrderDto>>
{
    public async Task<IReadOnlyList<OrderDto>> Handle(GetOrdersQuery request, CancellationToken ct)
    {
        var orders = await _repository.GetAllAsync(ct);
        return orders.Select(o => new OrderDto(o.Id, o.Name)).ToList();
    }
}
```

## What Kiro Must Never Do

- Rename layers or change the folder structure without an approved architecture proposal.
- Add NuGet packages not listed in the approved tech stack.
- Write business logic in ViewModels or XAML code-behind.
- Bypass the repository pattern with direct DbContext calls in Application.
- Add direct service-to-service references (use MediatR + shared contracts only).
- Delete or modify `openspec/` files outside the `openspec/changes/` flow.
- Create or write files under `.kiro/specs/` — all specification outputs must go to `openspec/changes/`.
